EXPERIMENT 36 – BLACK-BOX TESTING OF LOGIN REQUEST USING APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to execute black-box testing of a login request using the HTTP POST sampler.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter (jmeter.bat or jmeter.sh) and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add Thread Group under Test Plan.
3. Set:
   - Number of Threads = 3
   - Ramp-up Period = 3 seconds
   - Loop Count = 1
4. Add HTTP Cookie Manager because login uses a session.
5. Add an HTTP Request sampler with method POST and path /authenticate. Enter valid username and password. Select Follow Redirects.
6. Add a Response Assertion to check You logged into a secure area!.
7. Add a second HTTP Request with a wrong password and a Response Assertion to check Your password is invalid!.
8. Add View Results Tree and Summary Report. Run and verify both valid and invalid inputs.
INPUT – TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	3
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	3 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Cookie Manager	Default Settings	Added
HTTP Request 1	Server Name	the-internet.herokuapp.com
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	POST /authenticate
HTTP Request 1	Username	tomsmith
HTTP Request 1	Password	SuperSecretPassword!
HTTP Request 1	Follow Redirects	Selected
Response Assertion 1	Pattern	You logged into a secure area!
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	POST /authenticate
HTTP Request 2	Username	tomsmith
HTTP Request 2	Password	wrong123
HTTP Request 2	Follow Redirects	Selected
Response Assertion 2	Pattern	Your password is invalid!

OUTPUT
Summary Report
Label	Samples	Error %
Valid Login	3	0.00%
Invalid Password	3	0.00%
TOTAL	6	0.00%

Both groups are green because every response contains the expected message.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to execute black-box testing of a login request using the HTTP POST sampler and the results were verified.
